#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078256 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9afe0d46-84e7-5937-9b42-170097a72493" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Cosine"}] :question/id #uuid "17e8ec56-6fda-5294-b27c-9b3e312a5f75" :question/math-academy-id "e-3248" :question/problem "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{MN}$ rounded to one decimal place. \n\n![](images/db/db0c3be4d3f18a55bfbd763e4017bdabd6c27ba7b498e21909baa4aea3d44337.png)" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overline{NO}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overline{MN}$ adjacent to the given angle $\\angle{N}.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({25}^{∘}) & =\\frac{MN}{14} \\\\ MN & =14\\operatorname{cos}⁡({25}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN & =14\\operatorname{cos}⁡({25}^{∘}) \\\\  & =14(0.906\\,30…) \\\\  & =12.688\\,30… \\\\  & ≈12.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078257 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078551 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04354ab1-c6ec-534e-bb57-267f326c15fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Sine"}] :question/id #uuid "b4f8dd38-d62d-5940-b936-48f68e0693b8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3249" :question/problem "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{NO}$ rounded to one decimal place.\n\n![](images/91/9108818debc297388dde73a7aa7689eac263c6ec033643c7e2bcdfb3677a8f44.png)" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, notice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overline{MO}$ opposite the given angle $\\angle{N}$ and wish to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overline{NO}.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the hypotenuse is *sine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘}) & =\\frac{20}{NO} \\\\ NO\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘}) & =20 \\\\ NO & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}NO & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{(0.529\\,91…)} \\\\  & =37.741\\,59… \\\\  & ≈37.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078258 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "54289a8c-57cd-50b6-8b94-8628b2bc27be" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Tangent"}] :question/id #uuid "a74a938e-94a4-5a91-aced-4955dc8dfbf8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3250" :question/problem "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{BC}$ in terms of $\\theta.$\n\n![](images/8b/8b1f3d7e1d87c7021970f45279bb404b4e9998a9d351d1e95616dac98f80d45d.png)" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overline{AB}$ adjacent to the given angle $\\angle A$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overline{BC}$ opposite $\\angle A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =15\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078551 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04354ab1-c6ec-534e-bb57-267f326c15fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2329be16-9869-58b3-832e-c57647b69a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519047} {:answer/id #uuid "5a04c960-211f-5108-a49f-0a5ff1afbb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519128} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6afbe9-ac3a-5da9-89bf-afe8b4e58c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519134} {:answer/id #uuid "9957aacc-6748-5d81-bccb-17c654f8f56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519245} {:answer/id #uuid "b1822c7c-3f66-5e3b-9c5b-29a54cb930bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f6afbe9-ac3a-5da9-89bf-afe8b4e58c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519134} :answer-field/id #uuid "54e274fe-1093-5ef9-96b5-8767338dcb8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09ccf4cc-8d66-55a0-964d-b04cc4bd149d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122318" :question/problem "![](images/42/42d1bf23b4ce679748fb1c1765d568b0b32128155f3d6e7770a1b894b0888ded.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{LM}$ in terms of $\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{MN}$ opposite the given angle $m∠L$  and wish to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{LM}.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the hypotenuse is *sine*. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(m∠L) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{6}{LM} \\\\ LM\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =6 \\\\ LM & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "54289a8c-57cd-50b6-8b94-8628b2bc27be" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bbe2bc1-39d1-58da-9eea-f7dc76f0f445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519061} {:answer/id #uuid "4495747d-0147-5c33-a7dd-cc1052f4f100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519098} {:answer/id #uuid "7984a7a2-3d6d-5651-a31e-9d9abb8af095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519183} {:answer/id #uuid "c52fb001-1c61-5604-8c36-8c5eca7540da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519317} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4f9b02-26de-5ae1-8b55-ca9d1da42382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd4f9b02-26de-5ae1-8b55-ca9d1da42382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519326} :answer-field/id #uuid "b60226c5-c082-582a-8e44-74900cca7bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f70a7592-ca8c-59ec-84a8-2fae0d3e16cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-122357" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a9c863e0cdb9788e06c527e17207e87ba2281ab21c9bd0836009ca518a15631a.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to the given angle $∠C$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ opposite $∠C.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({56}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AB}{9} \\\\ AB & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡({56}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡({56}^{∘}) \\\\  & =9(1.482\\,56…) \\\\  & =13.343\\,04… \\\\  & ≈13.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "54289a8c-57cd-50b6-8b94-8628b2bc27be" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "072ae5a3-56fd-5113-989d-660f16471484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519001} {:answer/id #uuid "24a468a5-e58e-57bc-b82a-35381d14f313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519051} {:answer/id #uuid "31f46001-c019-5e7a-b980-818bd58d8124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519071} {:answer/id #uuid "45d6a559-84b7-5a2e-8ca5-baed1b46e2cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519102} {:answer/id #uuid "f74b5019-f040-540c-9f33-bd17a0a96652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a468a5-e58e-57bc-b82a-35381d14f313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519051} :answer-field/id #uuid "da843738-07b4-5faf-bd43-39de4fed6f05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ca7cacc-1a5f-515a-8db1-0999afb66a6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122362" :question/problem "![](images/80/804c19a20b6f47707a07c7bdcee3cbd727eec2c270109e30eb55d949ace8edf0.png)\n\nCalculate the value of $BC$ to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AC}$ opposite to the given angle $∠B$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent $∠B.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2.91}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) & =2.91 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{2.91}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\frac{2.91}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.91}{(0.363\\,97…)} \\\\  & =7.995\\,15… \\\\  & ≈8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9afe0d46-84e7-5937-9b42-170097a72493" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3255099-9357-5a64-bef8-7531c32dcdb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3255099-9357-5a64-bef8-7531c32dcdb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519393} :answer-field/id #uuid "43fabf49-a3c3-59b9-b08d-71606020d7d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65457b1f-86ca-5676-81db-c0f19c1bbed5" :question/math-academy-id "q-250820" :question/problem "A triangle $△ABC$ has $m∠A={38}^{∘},$ $m∠B={90}^{∘},$ and $AC=18.$ Find $AB$ rounded to the nearest integer.\n\n$AB≈${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the given triangle.\n\n![](images/d0/d097dca887930886a231b4b3a71e3236edcc25ec50a886f197a8c3111ff064fb.png)\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to the given angle $∠A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AB}{18} \\\\ AB & =18\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =18\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) \\\\  & =18(0.788\\,01…) \\\\  & =14.184\\,19… \\\\  & ≈14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078551 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04354ab1-c6ec-534e-bb57-267f326c15fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1b81862-5146-5f0a-8ac5-0fd79c0a2c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077469} {:answer/id #uuid "cf368945-778b-5d74-90d6-d2b82979f4cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077470} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7a84db-08fb-51e4-b38d-a6f78cb89655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077471} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed5b9e8-a40d-55c4-8a76-c92577e695bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077472} {:answer/id #uuid "36c4bd36-3076-50a5-a9a1-65ac22047faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed5b9e8-a40d-55c4-8a76-c92577e695bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077472} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd9bfa65-ff88-5011-a0c7-0a010f14b7ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07fbac6a-971f-53dc-a7f0-99a5c49ba233" :question/math-academy-id "q-54238" :question/problem "![](images/32/32938bfdcb2ed9130304722b408b304802062b701bb35c68d7d3333c7cfe8ee6.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ opposite the given angle $∠C.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the hypotenuse is *sine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({52}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AB}{15} \\\\ AB & =15\\operatorname{sin}⁡({52}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =15\\operatorname{sin}⁡({52}^{∘}) \\\\  & =15(0.788\\,01…) \\\\  & =11.820\\,16… \\\\  & ≈11.8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9afe0d46-84e7-5937-9b42-170097a72493" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c72506b-8c94-5289-96d5-369a216625af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519063} {:answer/id #uuid "7b799199-b32c-5119-bed5-f2daf8adb220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519186} {:answer/id #uuid "7c04ca98-cf65-54f5-b0a9-cdfa36672625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519188} {:answer/id #uuid "a25f7d74-887f-51bb-bf47-0e657f573c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519259} {:answer/id #uuid "c1510748-41d4-53d6-9916-52c67c514acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1510748-41d4-53d6-9916-52c67c514acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519311} :answer-field/id #uuid "e95f0005-9800-5362-8d1e-5d401889c55d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75f7a455-462c-51e4-9b1a-b0d79be3c2a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-54245" :question/problem "A triangle $△ABC$ has $m∠A={37}^{∘},$ $m∠B={90}^{∘},$ and $AC=25.$ Find $AB$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the given triangle.\n\n![](images/70/70ac3cbbc7209f71bd8095bb725d1dbb847c827bdfdc8220c25115fb120532b4.png)\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to the given angle $∠A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AB}{25} \\\\ AB & =25\\operatorname{cos}⁡({37}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =25\\operatorname{cos}⁡({37}^{∘}) \\\\  & =25(0.798\\,63…) \\\\  & =19.965\\,88… \\\\  & ≈20,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}]}
